00:15:11,677 --> 00:15:13,511
Wait a second.
There we go.

228
00:15:13,513 --> 00:15:15,780
All right. Good.

229
00:15:15,782 --> 00:15:17,782
--Hey, what the--

230
00:15:25,024 --> 00:15:27,258
hey, Earl.
You got a light?

231
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,093
Well--

232
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:31,462
oh, uh--
here.

233
00:15:32,531 --> 00:15:33,965
Ah, thank you.

234
00:15:43,610 --> 00:15:46,411
Stay down!
Stay down!

235
00:15:46,413 --> 00:15:48,012
Fire! Fire!
It's on fire.

236
00:15:56,055 --> 00:15:58,056
That is
massively stupid!

237
00:15:58,058 --> 00:16:00,325
That's
an $85,000 vehicle.

238
00:16:00,327 --> 00:16:02,727
Well,
he was assaulted.

239
00:16:02,729 --> 00:16:04,662
<i>He</i> tried
to assault<i> me.</i>

240
00:16:06,999 --> 00:16:09,901
Well, don't just
stand there gawping.
Get your phones out!

241
00:16:09,903 --> 00:16:11,970
Film this!
Document!

242
00:16:17,609 --> 00:16:18,943
Hey.
Aw--

243
00:16:18,945 --> 00:16:20,678
Christ!

244
00:16:26,418 --> 00:16:27,819
Cauliflower.

245
00:16:29,521 --> 00:16:32,423
- This is Max.
Get Mike on the phone.
- What'd he just say?

246
00:16:34,626 --> 00:16:37,495
Wait. Y-you can't
just walk away.
This is a crime scene.

247
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:40,531
Did you just say
"cauliflower" to me?

248
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:24,342
<i>Unless I'm mistaken,</i>

249
00:17:24,344 --> 00:17:28,913
yesterday, as you were
leavin' the bar, you said
the word "cauliflower."

250
00:17:29,748 --> 00:17:31,482
That's right. I did.

251
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:36,087
The last time
you said that word to me,

252
00:17:36,089 --> 00:17:38,689
I ended up
gettin' sent down
for six months.

253
00:17:38,691 --> 00:17:41,826
It was juvie.
I was 13.

254
00:17:41,828 --> 00:17:44,695
And you were supposed to be
the lookout, now, weren't you?

255
00:17:44,697 --> 00:17:46,831
Bein' that I was
your kid brother,

256
00:17:46,833 --> 00:17:50,902
I let you lead me into trouble
with all your crazy
cauliflower plans.

257
00:17:50,904 --> 00:17:53,071
My life of crime
is over.

258
00:17:54,273 --> 00:17:57,608
But you did
make breakfast
this morning.

259
00:17:57,610 --> 00:18:01,345
Even burned the bacon
like I like and you hate.

260
00:18:01,347 --> 00:18:04,682
I also saw you have
some sort of robbery
"to-do" list.

261
00:18:04,684 --> 00:18:09,554
Now, I know this attempt
to be organized
is a big step for you.

262
00:18:09,556 --> 00:18:10,922
So go.

263
00:18:16,228 --> 00:18:19,464
Charlotte motor speedway.

264
00:18:19,466 --> 00:18:21,632
The speedway.

265
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:30,575
<i>It's one of the busiest</i>
<i>sports venues in the country.</i>

266
00:18:30,577 --> 00:18:32,877
<i>Just last year</i>
<i>they had over 300 events.</i>

267
00:18:32,879 --> 00:18:36,914
<i>It's the official home</i>
<i>of nascar, of course. That's</i>
<i>all run on that main track.</i>

268
00:18:36,916 --> 00:18:41,619
<i>But that place right there</i>
<i>ain't just about racing.</i>
<i>This place is like a city.</i>

269
00:18:41,621 --> 00:18:43,721
<i>A few years ago</i>
<i>they built condos</i>

270
00:18:43,723 --> 00:18:45,656
<i>for people who wanted</i>
<i>to live above the track</i>
<i>all year long.</i>

271
00:18:45,658 --> 00:18:48,392
<i>They sold out</i>
<i>in less than 24 hours.</i>

272
00:18:48,394 --> 00:18:51,095
<i>They even got their own</i>
<i>police force and jail</i>
<i>for people carryin' on</i>

273
00:18:51,097 --> 00:18:53,564
<i>and gettin' out of hand.</i>

274
00:18:53,566 --> 00:18:56,267
Do you hear the words
comin' out your mouth?

275
00:18:56,269 --> 00:18:58,769
They have their own
police force.

276
00:18:58,771 --> 00:19:02,073
I'm midway
through my presentation,

277
00:19:02,075 --> 00:19:06,444
so you can just
not interrupt me
and let me get it out.

278
00:19:06,446 --> 00:19:09,847
How many times have I listened
to that "Logan family curse"
thing of yours?

279
00:19:12,918 --> 00:19:14,919
Thank you.

280
00:19:14,921 --> 00:19:18,789
Now,
as you very well know,

281
00:19:18,791 --> 00:19:22,093
speedway's got a big problem
on its hands night now.

282
00:19:22,095 --> 00:19:25,029
Forty-year-old pipe burst,
and since the whole thing
is built on landfill,

283
00:19:25,031 --> 00:19:27,331
it's turnin' to mush,
which is causin'
all these sinkholes.

284
00:19:27,333 --> 00:19:29,467
Sinkholes.
That's right.

285
00:19:29,469 --> 00:19:31,335
The sinkholes
in the infield.

286
00:19:31,337 --> 00:19:34,972
Now, they wanted
to fix this thing up right.
So what'd they do?

287
00:19:34,974 --> 00:19:38,142
What'd they do? They called
a bunch of us that used to
work down in them mines.

288
00:19:38,144 --> 00:19:39,710
'Cause we know the work.

289
00:19:44,349 --> 00:19:47,285
And you do
good work.
We do good work.

290
00:19:47,287 --> 00:19:50,621
But you
were just fired.

291
00:19:50,623 --> 00:19:54,625
I was let go
for liability reasons
involving insurance.

292
00:19:54,627 --> 00:19:58,095
Can you just get to the part
of why you think
you can do this?

293
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:01,732
I know how
they move the money.

294
00:20:15,414 --> 00:20:18,015
Who's got the code?
They can't get in!

295
00:20:18,017 --> 00:20:20,651
It's Christmas. "12-25."
That's the override.

296
00:20:20,653 --> 00:20:21,919
All right.

297
00:20:23,488 --> 00:20:25,256
I got a leg!
I got a leg!

298
00:20:25,258 --> 00:20:27,325
Give him some air.
Easy, easy,
easy, easy.

299
00:20:27,327 --> 00:20:29,260
All right.
Come on.

300
00:20:34,499 --> 00:20:37,668
Hey, bobo,
what the hell's
all this stuff?

301
00:20:37,670 --> 00:20:40,304
Well,
that's the ptt.

302
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:43,274
What, them--
they gas lines?

303
00:20:43,276 --> 00:20:44,609
Pneumatic
tube transport.

304
00:20:45,577 --> 00:20:47,878
Each concession
has its own rig.

305
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,914
When the register
starts to fill up,

306
00:20:49,916 --> 00:20:52,083
they can do
a money dump
through the ptt.

307
00:20:52,085 --> 00:20:56,187
Easy to do,
and it don't interfere
with the beer sellin'.

308
00:20:56,189 --> 00:21:00,224
Plus, heck of a lot more secure
than tryin' to pick up cash
during a race.

309
00:21:00,226 --> 00:21:03,728
So, all them pipes, what,
they just run right into--
to the main vault.

310
00:21:03,730 --> 00:21:06,764
The whole thing
is like a cash highway.

311
00:21:06,766 --> 00:21:08,766
<i>I even know</i>
<i>the when to do it.</i>

312
00:21:08,768 --> 00:21:11,135
June 4.
The grocery castle
auto show.

313
00:21:11,137 --> 00:21:14,739
It's graduation weekend.
It'll be the smallest
turnout of the summer.

314
00:21:14,741 --> 00:21:17,408
There gonna be
bare bones staff
and security.

315
00:21:17,410 --> 00:21:20,311
A real bank vault?

316
00:21:20,313 --> 00:21:23,948
Yeah, it's a tough one too.
I looked it up
on the Google.

317
00:21:29,321 --> 00:21:34,125
<i> The only guy</i>
<i>that knows anything about</i>
<i>blowin' up real bank vaults</i>

318
00:21:34,127 --> 00:21:36,727
<i>is Joe bang.</i>

319
00:21:36,729 --> 00:21:39,330
<i> Joe bang?</i>
<i>That's a legend right there.</i>

320
00:21:39,332 --> 00:21:42,033
<i>- You know where he is.</i>
<i>- No, I know where he is.</i>

321
00:21:43,135 --> 00:21:45,136
<i>We can't do it without him.</i>

322
00:21:51,943 --> 00:21:54,011
This is a surprise.

323
00:21:54,013 --> 00:21:56,013
What you say there,
Joe bang?

324
00:21:56,015 --> 00:21:59,183
Ain't seen you
in a while.
How goes it?

325
00:21:59,185 --> 00:22:03,454
Well, I'm sittin'
on this side of the table
wearin' a onesie.

326
00:22:03,456 --> 00:22:05,690
How do you think
it's goin'?

327
00:22:08,327 --> 00:22:09,860
Well,
you look good.

328
00:22:11,096 --> 00:22:14,031
Real good.
Fit.

329
00:22:17,135 --> 00:22:19,570
You two
got any quarters?

330
00:22:24,476 --> 00:22:26,210
I got a quarter.

331
00:22:26,212 --> 00:22:28,713
Does it have
to be a quarter?
Yeah.

332
00:22:28,715 --> 00:22:30,981
Come on now.
I found one.

333
00:22:30,983 --> 00:22:35,019
Yeah, well, one of you
go over to the machine
on the left, you punch j-7.

334
00:22:35,021 --> 00:22:36,887
Bring it back.
Go on, now.

335
00:22:50,569 --> 00:22:54,972
Doctors. They say
i have high blood pressure.

336
00:22:54,974 --> 00:22:58,376
So I get this
low-sodium salt
special.

337
00:22:59,244 --> 00:23:00,745
Fake salt.

338
00:23:03,081 --> 00:23:05,316
Can you believe that?

339
00:23:05,318 --> 00:23:07,251
Someone thought to do that.

340
00:23:08,387 --> 00:23:10,588
They make fake salt.

341
00:23:15,094 --> 00:23:16,894
So, you wanna
talk business?

342
00:23:16,896 --> 00:23:19,430
Well, we got
a job for you.

343
00:23:19,432 --> 00:23:20,798
A vault.

344
00:23:23,034 --> 00:23:25,903
Look around you,
my friends.

345
00:23:25,905 --> 00:23:28,773
My bank-blowin' days
are over.

346
00:23:30,041 --> 00:23:31,275
I...

347
00:23:31,277 --> 00:23:34,345
I got a little nest egg
waitin' for me

348
00:23:34,347 --> 00:23:35,946
when I get out.

349
00:23:37,349 --> 00:23:40,217
You're stashin'
$97,000?

350
00:23:40,219 --> 00:23:43,954
Buried under
the oak tree with the red swing
there at your place?

351
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:48,959
Maybe.

352
00:23:48,961 --> 00:23:53,497
It seems your brother fish
told his wife
about your stash.

353
00:23:56,735 --> 00:23:59,537
Fish told misty?
Yep.

354
00:23:59,539 --> 00:24:02,239
Next day misty
dug the whole thing up

355
00:24:02,241 --> 00:24:05,276
and ran off
with some truck driver
from Florida.

356
00:24:10,048 --> 00:24:12,082
What part of Florida?

357
00:24:12,084 --> 00:24:13,350
Clearwater.

358
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:17,288
It's a carven hill vault.

359
00:24:17,290 --> 00:24:20,057
Just like the one
you blew up
in parkersburg.

360
00:24:20,059 --> 00:24:23,461
Steel-encased concrete?
Yeah.
Wall's 20-inch thick.

361
00:24:23,463 --> 00:24:24,995
Alarms?

362
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:28,232
You sneeze
within ten feet

363
00:24:28,234 --> 00:24:30,334
of a carven hill
vault,

364
00:24:30,336 --> 00:24:33,237
its seismic sensors
will have you wearin'
one of these onesies

365
00:24:33,239 --> 00:24:34,972
before you know
what happened.

366
00:24:34,974 --> 00:24:38,242
Well, there's construction
goin' on round there right now,

367
00:24:38,244 --> 00:24:41,812
so them seismic sensors
are turned off.

368
00:24:43,583 --> 00:24:45,983
So we just need you
to blow her open.

369
00:24:45,985 --> 00:24:49,186
I got five months to go
in here.

370
00:24:50,856 --> 00:24:54,592
I should probably
lay low a bit
before doin' a job.

371
00:24:54,594 --> 00:24:57,194
This has to happen
in five weeks.

372
00:24:59,498 --> 00:25:01,298
I am...

373
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:04,568
Incar... cer...
Ra... Ted.

374
00:25:06,371 --> 00:25:09,340
Yeah, we got a... plan
to get you out.

375
00:25:19,951 --> 00:25:22,887
As in, break me out?

376
00:25:23,989 --> 00:25:25,256
Yep.

377
00:25:27,726 --> 00:25:30,327
In the middle of the night?

378
00:25:30,329 --> 00:25:32,530
No. Afternoon.

379
00:25:32,532 --> 00:25:34,265
It's a day job.

380
00:25:37,469 --> 00:25:42,339
You're gonna get me out of here
in broad daylight, do the job

381
00:25:42,341 --> 00:25:45,910
and then get me back in here
before anyone notices?

382
00:25:48,013 --> 00:25:49,947
Yup.

383
00:25:53,818 --> 00:25:55,553
You logans

384
00:25:55,555 --> 00:25:58,923
must be as simpleminded
as people say.

385
00:25:59,858 --> 00:26:01,759
People say that?

386
00:26:01,761 --> 00:26:04,261
Who?

387
00:26:05,063 --> 00:26:06,263
So...

388
00:26:07,265 --> 00:26:09,333
What's the take?

389
00:26:09,335 --> 00:26:12,336
It's bigger'n you can bury under an oak tree.
And the split?

390
00:26:12,338 --> 00:26:14,405
Even split.
No. No way.

391
00:26:16,341 --> 00:26:18,409
Well, why not?

392
00:26:19,344 --> 00:26:21,912
I got a brother.
I got two.

393
00:26:21,914 --> 00:26:24,448
I'd need 'em involved
to protect my interest.

394
00:26:43,034 --> 00:26:45,970
Say, why don't you take these
over to your mama?

395
00:26:45,972 --> 00:26:47,871
I'll bring the rest.

396
00:26:47,873 --> 00:26:50,908
When you gonna give
that piece of junk up? Huh?

397
00:26:50,910 --> 00:26:53,911
I keep telling you to
come down to the dealership
and I'll hook you up.

398
00:26:53,913 --> 00:26:55,613
You know
we're family.

399
00:26:55,615 --> 00:26:57,715
We're not family.

400
00:26:57,717 --> 00:27:00,818
You mean,
i can't interest you
in the latest v6 offering

401
00:27:00,820 --> 00:27:03,053
of the American
classic mustang?

402
00:27:03,055 --> 00:27:05,990
3.7 liters
of pure power.

403
00:27:05,992 --> 00:27:07,825
Come on.

404
00:27:07,827 --> 00:27:10,728
You can't tell me
you wouldn't love to get
behind the wheel of this baby.

405
00:27:10,730 --> 00:27:12,997
Come on, jump on in.
Take it for a spin.

406
00:27:12,999 --> 00:27:15,833
I don't need anything
that fancy.

407
00:27:15,835 --> 00:27:18,769
Well, you know
this Nova ended up
costin' Chevy a ton.

408
00:27:18,771 --> 00:27:21,572
It totally
bit the dust
in Mexico.

409
00:27:21,574 --> 00:27:25,476
You know,
in Mexican "Nova"
translates to "no go."

410
00:27:25,478 --> 00:27:27,511
They couldn't
get anyone
to buy it

411
00:27:27,513 --> 00:27:30,948
'cause they all thought
the car would, you know,
no go.

412
00:27:30,950 --> 00:27:32,816
You're an idiot.
No, it's true.

413
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:35,519
Not true.
Look it up.

414
00:27:36,988 --> 00:27:40,357
I am kinda surprised
you went for the v6 automatic.

415
00:27:40,359 --> 00:27:44,261
The v8's just so much faster,
and you can really feel
the road under you.

416
00:27:44,263 --> 00:27:46,430
Course, I keep forgettin',
you can't drive stick.

417
00:27:46,432 --> 00:27:49,133
No, i-i know how
to drive stick.
I don't think you do.

418
00:27:49,135 --> 00:27:52,169
All the cars you always
bringin' home from the lot
are auto.

419
00:27:52,171 --> 00:27:54,438
I love stick.
I'm a big fan of stick!

420
00:28:25,003 --> 00:28:27,938
Whoo-hoo!

421
00:28:29,708 --> 00:28:32,242
Yeah! Yeah! Go!
Come on!
Come on!

422
00:28:35,313 --> 00:28:37,347
Come on, come on, come on!

423
00:28:40,419 --> 00:28:43,253
Come on, girl!
Let's go!
Go, Sadie!

424
00:28:44,389 --> 00:28:46,090
Whoo-ooh!

425
00:28:46,092 --> 00:28:48,892
You got a ribbon, baby.
Come here. What's it say?

426
00:28:48,894 --> 00:28:51,862
It's not first place.
It only matters
if you win.

427
00:28:51,864 --> 00:28:54,264
What?
That ain't true at all.

428
00:28:54,266 --> 00:28:56,533
That boy's
damn near 14 years old.

429
00:28:56,535 --> 00:28:58,635
Come on.
Give me a smile.

430
00:28:59,537 --> 00:29:01,138
Go show your mama.

431
00:29:03,508 --> 00:29:06,043
Good job, baby doll.
Come to mama.

432
00:29:06,045 --> 00:29:07,511
Thanks.
Aww.

433
00:29:07,513 --> 00:29:09,413
You did good!
Let me see.

434
00:29:10,882 --> 00:29:12,449
Well,
i found 'em.

435
00:29:13,618 --> 00:29:15,452
Where?

436
00:29:15,454 --> 00:29:17,521
You should see.

437
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:30,134
They'll know
what we want them to know.

438
00:29:35,540 --> 00:29:37,875
<i>Let's hear it for</i>
<i>the bang brothers, folks!</i>

439
00:29:42,914 --> 00:29:45,149
Aw, dang.
Y'all got a sec?

440
00:29:45,151 --> 00:29:47,151
Whoa, whoa.
I'm winnin'.

441
00:29:48,052 --> 00:29:49,620
Okay?
Not stoppin'.

442
00:29:49,622 --> 00:29:52,923
Don't you put
the Logan hex on me.

443
00:29:52,925 --> 00:29:54,958
Yeah, we been out
to see your brother.

444
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:57,461
He tell you
that we're lookin'
to talk to y'all?

445
00:29:57,463 --> 00:30:00,464
Joe said
you need for him to
blow open the vault.

446
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:05,636
Somethin' like that.
Mm-hmm.

447
00:30:07,906 --> 00:30:10,641
Joe said
you know computers.
Yeah.

448
00:30:10,643 --> 00:30:14,111
I went to, uh,
technical college.

449
00:30:14,113 --> 00:30:16,814
Well, this here's
a little more involved
than that.

450
00:30:16,816 --> 00:30:18,816
We need, like,
a computer whiz.

451
00:30:18,818 --> 00:30:20,918
Like one of them
Facebook boys.

452
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:23,954
I know everything
there is to know
about computers, okay.

453
00:30:23,956 --> 00:30:25,756
All the twitters.
I know 'em.

454
00:30:25,758 --> 00:30:27,925
But me and Sam
just ain't sure
we can help y'all.

455
00:30:28,993 --> 00:30:30,961
You can't help us?
Yeah.

456
00:30:30,963 --> 00:30:34,097
We're livin'
with the lord now.

457
00:30:34,099 --> 00:30:37,367
Which means
on the light side
of the raw.
Mm-hmm.

458
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:43,373
If you two ain't into this,
then why the hell did Joe
tell us to come out here then?

459
00:30:43,375 --> 00:30:45,943
