1140
01:28:34,076 --> 01:28:37,911
For her talent,
Sadie Logan will perform
"umbrella" by Rihanna.

1141
01:29:17,151 --> 01:29:19,786
I picked this song

1142
01:29:19,788 --> 01:29:21,688
'cause it's
my daddy's favorite.

1143
01:31:01,557 --> 01:31:03,290
Where you gonna put it?

1144
01:31:03,292 --> 01:31:05,158
I can make
a trophy case.

1145
01:31:05,160 --> 01:31:07,327
You're gonna need to now.
You've got so many.
All right.

1146
01:31:07,329 --> 01:31:09,129
Give me a hug.

1147
01:31:09,131 --> 01:31:11,298
I love you, daddy.
I love you too.

1148
01:31:11,300 --> 01:31:14,067
Let me see
the gun show.

1149
01:31:14,069 --> 01:31:15,602
All right.
All right, Jo.
I love you.

1150
01:31:15,604 --> 01:31:18,071
Love you.
See you, Jimmy.

1151
01:31:18,073 --> 01:31:20,907
See you back at home,
baby.
All right.

1152
01:31:22,777 --> 01:31:24,711
What the heck?

1153
01:31:26,280 --> 01:31:28,682
What the hell happened
to my car?

1154
01:31:32,954 --> 01:31:34,855
Are you kidding me?

1155
01:31:46,000 --> 01:31:48,535
Hey, partner.
Where you headed to?

1156
01:31:50,304 --> 01:31:54,007
All the way through?
Mind if I catch a ride
with you?

1157
01:31:54,009 --> 01:31:56,576
You sure, man?
I ain't puttin' you out
or nothin'?

1158
01:32:43,724 --> 01:32:46,526
<i>Authorities have confirmed they</i>
<i>have recovered the money stolen</i>

1159
01:32:46,528 --> 01:32:48,395
<i>from the Charlotte</i>
<i>motor speedway,</i>

1160
01:32:48,397 --> 01:32:50,931
<i>in what some are calling</i>
<i>the "hillbilly heist."</i>

1161
01:32:50,933 --> 01:32:54,534
<i>Sources say an anonymous caller</i>
<i>led police to this gas station</i>

1162
01:32:54,536 --> 01:32:58,738
<i>where they discovered</i>
<i>an abandoned truck</i>
<i>containing bags of cash</i>

1163
01:32:58,740 --> 01:33:02,676
<i>that have been positively linked</i>
<i>to the robbery over the weekend.</i>

1164
01:33:02,678 --> 01:33:06,212
<i>The truck was reported stolen</i>
<i>last week.</i>

1165
01:33:06,214 --> 01:33:09,683
<i>Our forensic team</i>
<i>is at work on the scene.</i>

1166
01:33:09,685 --> 01:33:11,518
<i>And we're certain</i>
<i>they'll find--</i>

1167
01:33:11,520 --> 01:33:13,587
why go to all the trouble
to rob a place

1168
01:33:13,589 --> 01:33:15,722
if you don't have the guts
to keep the money?

1169
01:33:15,724 --> 01:33:17,624
He must've chickened out.

1170
01:33:19,694 --> 01:33:22,295
<i> We are joined now</i>
<i> by a resident daredevil</i>

1171
01:33:22,297 --> 01:33:24,297
<i> at little victories</i>
<i> animal shelter.</i>

1172
01:33:24,299 --> 01:33:27,133
<i>This is Josh morrison.</i>
<i>Thank you for joining us today.</i>

1173
01:33:27,135 --> 01:33:30,470
<i> Right.
He comes on</i> <i>about-- he used to come on a lot</i> <i>on</i> midday<i> for pet of the week.</i>

1174
01:33:30,472 --> 01:33:33,273
<i>So he's joining us to talk</i>
<i>about a new adoption challenge</i>

1175
01:33:33,275 --> 01:33:36,309
<i>at the shelter</i>
<i>for little victories.</i>
<i>We do have to talk about the--</i>

1176
01:34:10,745 --> 01:34:13,146
<i>well, we brought everyone in</i>
<i>at 6:00 this morning.</i>

1177
01:34:13,148 --> 01:34:16,316
Couldn't work all weekend,
you know, 'cause of the race,
obviously.

1178
01:34:16,318 --> 01:34:18,852
But everything was just
like we left it on Friday.

1179
01:34:18,854 --> 01:34:21,087
How many men do you have
working today?

1180
01:34:21,089 --> 01:34:24,758
Oh, 40 or so.
I guess we're on a bit
of a tight deadline

1181
01:34:24,760 --> 01:34:27,427
'cause we're trying
to get everything shored up

1182
01:34:27,429 --> 01:34:29,195
since the season's
startin'.

1183
01:34:29,197 --> 01:34:31,398
We'll be wrappin'
outta here this week.

1184
01:34:32,933 --> 01:34:35,835
I'm gonna need prints
from all your guys.

1185
01:34:35,837 --> 01:34:40,273
Well, sure, but, well,
all the workers have to wear
protective gloves at all times.

1186
01:34:40,275 --> 01:34:43,610
That's--
well, that's a union rule.
Union rule.

1187
01:34:43,612 --> 01:34:45,545
Yep.
Great.

1188
01:34:45,547 --> 01:34:49,549
Agent Grayson.
Local pd got a call from someone
claiming to be an eyewitness.

1189
01:34:49,551 --> 01:34:53,553
Swears they saw the robbers,
can definitely identify 'em.

1190
01:34:53,555 --> 01:34:56,523
Yeah, I saw 'em.
I know who they are too.

1191
01:34:56,525 --> 01:34:58,658
Why don't we start
at the beginning?

1192
01:34:58,660 --> 01:35:00,960
Where'd you see them?
In a tunnel.

1193
01:35:00,962 --> 01:35:03,697
Leading from the track
back to the shower room
and the lockers.

1194
01:35:03,699 --> 01:35:06,499
<i> There's</i>
<i> a saying in our business.</i>
<i> "Set it up and shut up."</i>

1195
01:35:06,501 --> 01:35:09,135
<i>So I'll shut up.</i>

1196
01:35:09,137 --> 01:35:13,206
<i>What the hell was that?</i>
<i>You call yourself a driver?</i>

1197
01:35:13,208 --> 01:35:15,075
<i>What, you never been boxed</i>
<i>in a turn before?</i>

1198
01:35:15,077 --> 01:35:16,976
<i> I told you I didn't want</i>
<i> to drink your poison.</i>

1199
01:35:16,978 --> 01:35:19,479
<i> I thought I was having</i>
<i> a heart attack!</i>
<i>That poison is saving your--</i>

1200
01:35:19,481 --> 01:35:22,649
can't one of you hit "mute"?
I'm tryin' to give my statement
to the FBI here.

1201
01:35:22,651 --> 01:35:25,051
<i> You drink what I say.</i>
<i> You drive how I say.</i>

1202
01:35:25,053 --> 01:35:28,555
There was two of 'em. Right?
Now, one of 'em was a bartender
from that place out off of i-17.

1203
01:35:28,557 --> 01:35:31,825
Got one arm.
The guy with him,
i don't know who he was.

1204
01:35:31,827 --> 01:35:33,893
And you know
the bartender from?

1205
01:35:33,895 --> 01:35:36,663
A while back,
i got in a fight at the bar.
With the bartender?

1206
01:35:36,665 --> 01:35:38,398
No, with his brother.

1207
01:35:38,400 --> 01:35:42,736
-Did the brother
have one arm or two?
-The brother's got both.

1208
01:35:42,738 --> 01:35:45,905
And the fight was about?
I can't remember.

1209
01:35:45,907 --> 01:35:49,375
And you won that fight
at the bar?
Hell, yeah, I won it.

1210
01:35:49,377 --> 01:35:52,245
So you saw the bartender
with one arm

1211
01:35:52,247 --> 01:35:55,548
and an unknown male companion
in the tunnel during the race?

1212
01:35:55,550 --> 01:35:58,017
And they were?

1213
01:35:58,019 --> 01:36:02,455
Well, they was just walkin',
but it was suspicious-like.

1214
01:36:02,457 --> 01:36:04,524
Suspicious how?

1215
01:36:04,526 --> 01:36:07,594
Well, they shouldn't
have been down there.
That was suspicious.

1216
01:36:07,596 --> 01:36:10,296
But you didn't think
to mention this encounter
to anyone

1217
01:36:10,298 --> 01:36:12,966
until you saw the news
on the television
about the robbery?

1218
01:36:12,968 --> 01:36:16,369
The docs had to
set my nose, all right?
I've been in recovery.

1219
01:36:16,371 --> 01:36:20,640
So all of these injuries are
the result of your latest fight
with the brothers?

1220
01:36:20,642 --> 01:36:23,910
Bartender brother.
He's the one that punched me
in the tunnel.

1221
01:36:23,912 --> 01:36:27,213
-The one-armed--
-yeah, look, just ask my driver,
Dayton white. Right?

1222
01:36:27,215 --> 01:36:29,649
He was with me
when all this went down.
He'll back up my story.

1223
01:36:31,218 --> 01:36:33,219
Yes, when you called in
your tip, you mentioned

1224
01:36:33,221 --> 01:36:36,556
that he'd be able
to corroborate your story.

1225
01:36:36,558 --> 01:36:39,826
We spoke with Dayton white
earlier today.

1226
01:36:39,828 --> 01:36:42,929
He stated he was never
in the tunnel with you
during the race.

1227
01:36:42,931 --> 01:36:46,266
Never saw two suspicious men.

1228
01:36:46,268 --> 01:36:48,668
And has no idea what
you're talking about.

1229
01:37:11,458 --> 01:37:13,426
Did you talk to him?

1230
01:37:13,428 --> 01:37:15,528
I think he knows better.

1231
01:37:25,039 --> 01:37:28,474
I stopped by the trailer
when he wasn't home.

1232
01:37:28,476 --> 01:37:31,644
I think I got most
of your stuff.

1233
01:37:31,646 --> 01:37:33,713
You sure love
your books.

1234
01:37:35,049 --> 01:37:36,950
And there's some mail
there too.

1235
01:38:08,916 --> 01:38:12,886
Visitation logs indicate
that Jimmy Logan,

1236
01:38:12,888 --> 01:38:16,022
an employee recently fired
from the speedway,

1237
01:38:16,024 --> 01:38:19,092
came with his brother Clyde
to see Joseph bang

1238
01:38:19,094 --> 01:38:21,160
here on April 15.

1239
01:38:21,162 --> 01:38:23,663
Hmm.
They returned two days later
for a second visit.

1240
01:38:23,665 --> 01:38:28,234
Now, we only have video
of this meeting, no audio,

1241
01:38:28,236 --> 01:38:30,904
so we have no idea
what they discussed.

1242
01:38:30,906 --> 01:38:33,072
But the following week,

1243
01:38:33,074 --> 01:38:36,676
Clyde Logan drives
through the window
of a corner save mart

1244
01:38:36,678 --> 01:38:40,113
and ends up being sentenced
to 90 days here.

1245
01:38:40,115 --> 01:38:43,616
You seem to have
a lot of information
in your FBI folders there.

1246
01:38:46,787 --> 01:38:50,256
-And so?
-You don't think that's
an incredible coincidence?

1247
01:38:53,727 --> 01:38:56,629
No. Not really.

1248
01:38:56,631 --> 01:39:00,300
I mean, if you're askin' me,
am I shocked that the criminals
locked up in here

1249
01:39:00,302 --> 01:39:04,771
are friends
with other criminals,
no, I'm not.

1250
01:39:08,409 --> 01:39:12,045
So Clyde Logan and Joseph bang
were incarcerated here,
at your prison,

1251
01:39:12,047 --> 01:39:14,080
on may the 28th,

1252
01:39:14,082 --> 01:39:19,118
and you had no problems,
no issues of any kind
at your prison on that day.

1253
01:39:19,120 --> 01:39:22,221
Is that right?
No. Uh-uh. We didn't
have any problems.

1254
01:39:22,223 --> 01:39:24,624
Right. 'Cause Monroe county
fire department said

1255
01:39:24,626 --> 01:39:27,961
that they dispatched
multiple units
around 8:30 P.M. that night.

1256
01:39:27,963 --> 01:39:30,563
There was a small
kitchen fire,

1257
01:39:30,565 --> 01:39:33,566
but that's not a problem
in the context of this prison.

1258
01:39:33,568 --> 01:39:36,169
I mean, it's standard
operating procedure

1259
01:39:36,171 --> 01:39:39,272
for them to dispatch
multiple units

1260
01:39:39,274 --> 01:39:41,474
any time there's a fire
at the prison.

1261
01:39:41,476 --> 01:39:45,812
That was no big deal.
It was out within a few minutes.

1262
01:39:49,583 --> 01:39:53,586
You certain that
these two inmates couldn't
have broken out of here,

1263
01:39:53,588 --> 01:39:57,824
robbed the speedway and then
broken back into your prison
without you knowing about it?

1264
01:39:57,826 --> 01:40:00,259
Wow!

1265
01:40:00,261 --> 01:40:02,595
No.

1266
01:40:02,597 --> 01:40:05,531
Agent Grayson,
I've been warden here
for nine years,

1267
01:40:05,533 --> 01:40:08,668
and I can tell you this.

1268
01:40:08,670 --> 01:40:11,571
We don't have
an escape problem at Monroe.

1269
01:40:13,107 --> 01:40:15,008
<i> What do you</i>
<i>think of the robbery?</i>

1270
01:40:15,010 --> 01:40:18,478
<i> Well, I heard that</i>
<i> they're callin' it</i>
<i> "ocean's 7-Eleven"</i>

1271
01:40:18,480 --> 01:40:22,015
<i> 'cause they found</i>
<i> that truck with the money</i>
<i> behind a convenience store.</i>

1272
01:40:22,017 --> 01:40:24,884
<i> Uh, I heard</i>
<i> that they're callin' 'em</i>
<i> the "redneck robbers"</i>

1273
01:40:24,886 --> 01:40:28,321
<i> because they think the guys</i>
<i> who did this whole thing</i>
<i> are from around here.</i>

1274
01:40:28,323 --> 01:40:30,056
<i> I hope</i>
<i> they never catch 'em.</i>

1275
01:40:30,058 --> 01:40:32,191
<i> Where does</i>
<i> this investigation stand?</i>

1276
01:40:32,193 --> 01:40:35,028
<i> Let me tell you this.
</i> <i> Even though the crime</i> <i> was committed in Charlotte,</i>

1277
01:40:35,030 --> 01:40:39,465
<i>the fact that the money</i>
<i>was recovered here</i>
<i>makes it a very serious matter.</i>

1278
01:40:39,467 --> 01:40:42,368
<i>We're involving</i>
<i>all of our local, state</i>
<i>and federal officials.</i>

1279
01:40:42,370 --> 01:40:45,505
You have a problem
with the food here, inmate?
No, no, no, warden.

1280
01:40:45,507 --> 01:40:47,640
N-no problem.

1281
01:40:47,642 --> 01:40:50,576
Reckon your stomach's not
been botherin' you lately?

1282
01:40:50,578 --> 01:40:52,545
No, warden, no.

1283
01:40:52,547 --> 01:40:54,480
Th-thank you
for asking me.

1284
01:40:59,520 --> 01:41:02,822
You best be
cleaning up your mess.

1285
01:41:02,824 --> 01:41:05,258
Now.
Sure.

1286
01:41:08,595 --> 01:41:10,096
Huh?

1287
01:41:16,670 --> 01:41:18,604
What'd you say to me,
inmate?

1288
01:41:20,541 --> 01:41:22,075
Go on.

1289
01:41:24,611 --> 01:41:26,646
Thank you.

1290
01:41:28,850 --> 01:41:31,751
<i>What about the disgruntled</i>
<i>fired employee?</i>

1291
01:41:31,753 --> 01:41:33,886
<i>The brother</i>
<i>of the one-armed bartender?</i>

1292
01:41:33,888 --> 01:41:37,123
Jimmy Logan
was fired six weeks
before the robbery.

1293
01:41:37,125 --> 01:41:39,625
His brother, Clyde,
is the one-armed bartender

1294
01:41:39,627 --> 01:41:43,229
Max chilblain claims to
have seen during the race.

1295
01:41:43,231 --> 01:41:47,066
But we know there's no way
Clyde Logan could have been
in that underground walkway

1296
01:41:47,068 --> 01:41:50,069
because he was serving time
at the Monroe correctional
facility

1297
01:41:50,071 --> 01:41:52,638
on the day of the robbery.

1298
01:41:52,640 --> 01:41:54,140
Hmm.

1299
01:41:56,643 --> 01:41:59,812
I hate airtight alibis.

1300
01:41:59,814 --> 01:42:02,648
Where did Jimmy Logan's
cell phone tell us he was
during the race?

1301
01:42:02,650 --> 01:42:04,784
Jimmy Logan doesn't
have a cell phone.

1302
01:42:04,786 --> 01:42:07,620
Shut off three months ago
for nonpayment.

1303
01:42:07,622 --> 01:42:13,259
He also drives
a 1983 Ford f150,
so no GPS.

1304
01:42:13,261 --> 01:42:16,429
No e-mail.
No social media.

1305
01:42:16,431 --> 01:42:19,298
We did get a few hits
on his name on other
social media accounts,

1306
01:42:19,300 --> 01:42:22,835
which place him
at valley view high school
during the race.

1307
01:42:22,837 --> 01:42:26,405
His daughter was competing
in the miss pretty West Virginia
pageant.

1308
01:42:26,407 --> 01:42:28,541
And apparently,
she won.

1309
01:43:05,446 --> 01:43:07,413
How's your brother?

1310
01:43:09,116 --> 01:43:11,083
I wouldn't know.

1311
01:43:12,352 --> 01:43:14,554
You haven't
talked to him?
Nope.

1312
01:43:17,291 --> 01:43:19,692
Not once?

1313
01:43:19,694 --> 01:43:21,194
Nope.

1314
01:43:22,829 --> 01:43:26,399
Well, seems strange--
you know,

1315
01:43:26,401 --> 01:43:28,734
you two being so close
and all.

1316
01:43:30,971 --> 01:43:34,073
Last I heard, he moved south
to be closer to his daughter.

1317
01:43:38,012 --> 01:43:39,979
How far south?

1318
01:43:39,981 --> 01:43:41,547
Lynchburg.

1319
01:43:44,585 --> 01:43:49,255
Guess his ex moved down there
when her husband opened
a new car lot.

1320
01:43:54,094 --> 01:43:56,195
Well...

1321
01:43:56,197 --> 01:43:59,065
If you do speak
to him...

1322
01:44:02,369 --> 01:44:04,837
Tell him I'd like
to talk to him.

1323
01:44:04,839 --> 01:44:07,340
I doubt
I'll be talkin' to him.

1324
01:44:21,122 --> 01:44:25,591
He never told you why
he gave all that money back?

1325
01:44:35,536 --> 01:44:37,236
On the house.

1326
01:44:40,474 --> 01:44:42,541
Generous.

1327
01:44:45,213 --> 01:44:49,715
You've had your six months,
and you made no arrests.

1328
01:44:49,717 --> 01:44:54,453
Meanwhile, the locals talk
about these thieves like they're
some type of<i> hee haw</i> heroes.

1329
01:44:54,455 --> 01:44:56,622
So,

1330
01:44:56,624 --> 01:45:01,394
we would like to move forward
and put this entire incident
in our rearview mirror,

1331
01:45:01,396 --> 01:45:03,396
if you will.

1332
01:45:03,398 --> 01:45:04,864
Okay.

1333
01:45:12,072 --> 01:45:14,006
Thank you again.

1334
01:45:15,142 --> 01:45:16,976
I do have
one last question.

1335
01:45:17,978 --> 01:45:19,745
Sure.

1336
01:45:19,747 --> 01:45:22,315
You just said
you received a payout
from your insurance company

1337
01:45:22,317 --> 01:45:24,350
for the money
that wasn't recovered.

1338
01:45:24,352 --> 01:45:26,085
Yes, that's right.

1339
01:45:26,087 --> 01:45:28,087
Hmm.

1340
01:45:28,089 --> 01:45:31,457
We were here
with forensic accountants
for weeks,

1341
01:45:31,459 --> 01:45:34,960
poring over
the register logs
and receipts.

1342
01:45:34,962 --> 01:45:37,797
No one here was ever able
to give us an exact accounting

1343
01:45:37,799 --> 01:45:39,565
of how much money
was actually stolen.

1344
01:45:40,367 --> 01:45:42,134
Right. Uh--

1345
01:45:42,136 --> 01:45:45,104
well, it's very complex--
the algorithm and whatnot.

1346
01:45:45,106 --> 01:45:47,373
Yeah, we heard about
the complicated algorithms.

1347
01:45:48,675 --> 01:45:51,711
So how'd you arrive
at the number to ask for

1348
01:45:51,713 --> 01:45:53,913
if you didn't know
how much was stolen?

1349
01:45:55,315 --> 01:45:57,049
I'm not an accountant,

1350
01:45:57,051 --> 01:46:00,786
so, uh, I wasn't in there
for those discussions.

1351
01:46:00,788 --> 01:46:05,224
But as far as all of us here
at Charlotte motor speedway
are concerned,

1352
01:46:05,226 --> 01:46:08,361
the matter has been resolved
to our satisfaction.

1353
01:46:48,069 --> 01:46:49,502
Assholes.

1354
01:47:36,217 --> 01:47:41,220
You seriously want
to trust these two
with our lives?

1355
01:47:41,222 --> 01:47:43,622
They gonna know
what we want 'em to know.

1356
01:48:26,868 --> 01:48:29,168
- All right.
-But we can get two more.

1357
01:48:29,170 --> 01:48:31,770
What's rule eight?
Don't get greedy.

1358
01:48:31,772 --> 01:48:34,874
All right. You're done here.
Come on, you gotta get
the car anyway. Go.

1359
01:49:28,695 --> 01:49:32,231
Yeah, you're right there.
You're right on top of it.
Just dig in there.

1360
01:49:45,846 --> 01:49:47,546
Mr. naaman?

1361
01:49:53,754 --> 01:49:55,888
Came in through
the donation box.

1362
01:49:55,890 --> 01:49:58,857
It's heavy,
but don't get excited.

1363
01:49:58,859 --> 01:50:02,428
It's gotta be from a crazy,
written with crayon.
Know what I mean?

1364
01:51:02,122 --> 01:51:05,324
Hey.
Hi.

1365
01:51:05,326 --> 01:51:07,326
New job?

1366
01:51:07,328 --> 01:51:10,295
Yeah. It's just seasonal.

1367
01:51:10,297 --> 01:51:13,499
I hope they keep me on though.
It's nice being close to home.

1368
01:51:14,367 --> 01:51:16,035
You want to come in?

1369
01:51:16,037 --> 01:51:18,504
No, no. I'll just wait.

1370
01:51:18,506 --> 01:51:19,972
Daddy!
Hey! What's up, man?

1371
01:51:19,974 --> 01:51:22,341
Oh!
Body slam!

1372
01:51:22,343 --> 01:51:25,344
What time
you want her back?

1373
01:51:25,346 --> 01:51:27,379
Whatever time
works best for you.

1374
01:51:27,381 --> 01:51:29,348
We're just around.
All right.

1375
01:51:29,350 --> 01:51:30,883
Don't wait up!

1376
01:51:32,519 --> 01:51:36,021
All right.
So I was thinkin'...
Putt-putt golf.

1377
01:51:36,023 --> 01:51:38,123
They got those new
go-karts down there.

1378
01:51:38,125 --> 01:51:40,459
Sure. As long
as we get gelato after.

1379
01:51:40,461 --> 01:51:41,794
Gelato?
Yeah.

1380
01:51:41,796 --> 01:51:43,996
Ain't that
like fancy ice cream?

1381
01:51:43,998 --> 01:51:47,566
I thought you couldn't do that,
'cause of your pageants.
Oh, I'm over all that stuff.

1382
01:51:47,568 --> 01:51:50,235
I've been really getting into
the culinary arts lately.

1383
01:51:50,237 --> 01:51:52,504
The culi-what?

1384
01:51:52,506 --> 01:51:56,208
Cooking!
I've been watching
a lot of<i> top chef.</i>

1385
01:51:56,210 --> 01:51:58,877
Really?
Yeah, I've been
learnin' a lot.

1386
01:51:58,879 --> 01:52:01,914
Like how gelato isn't
just fancy ice cream.

1387
01:52:01,916 --> 01:52:05,584
It's made at a slower
churn rate than ice cream,
so less air gets mixed in.

1388
01:52:05,586 --> 01:52:08,687
That's why it has
such a silky texture.

1389
01:52:08,689 --> 01:52:10,989
A "churn rate," huh?
Yeah, a churn rate.

1390
01:52:10,991 --> 01:52:13,392
How fast the paddle
in the machine moves.

1391
01:52:13,394 --> 01:52:16,028
Sometimes the paddle
is called a dasher.

1392
01:52:16,030 --> 01:52:18,497
Oh, yeah, no,
i know what that is.

1393
01:52:18,499 --> 01:52:23,569
A dasher.
It's kinda like dasher
and dancer and ViXen.

1394
01:52:23,571 --> 01:52:25,437
No, daddy!

1395
01:52:25,439 --> 01:52:27,272
I know exactly
what that is.
No, it's not that.

1396
01:52:27,274 --> 01:52:29,675
I didn't know that reindeer
made ice cream.

1397
01:52:29,677 --> 01:52:31,143
They don't!

1398
01:52:33,079 --> 01:52:36,381
You funny.
You funny.
You funny-lookin'.

1399
01:52:46,459 --> 01:52:49,027
You never told me how
you knew the coast was clear

1400
01:52:49,029 --> 01:52:52,598
and we could
go get the money.

1401
01:52:52,600 --> 01:52:56,535
Well, you know how that phone
company give you about 60 days
to pay that phone bill?

1402
01:52:56,537 --> 01:53:01,373
Yeah.
Well, you go one day over,
and they shut your phone off.

1403
01:53:01,375 --> 01:53:05,244
So?

1404
01:53:05,246 --> 01:53:08,947
I ain't paid the bill
out at the trailer
in, like, six months.

1405
01:53:08,949 --> 01:53:11,049
So?

1406
01:53:11,051 --> 01:53:14,253
Figured long as they
was tappin' my phone,
they'd keep it on.

1407
01:53:14,255 --> 01:53:17,022
About a week ago,
it finally went dead.

1408
01:53:20,460 --> 01:53:22,728
That's pretty good.
Yeah.

1409
01:53:22,730 --> 01:53:25,931
You came up with that
on your own?
Yes, I did.

1410
01:53:25,933 --> 01:53:28,801
Well, that's a lot
of thinkin' for a Logan.

1411
01:53:40,647 --> 01:53:42,548
Hey, Jimmy.
Hey.

1412
01:53:43,850 --> 01:53:45,584
What you doin'?

1413
01:53:45,586 --> 01:53:47,653
A bit much?
No shit it was.

1414
01:53:47,655 --> 01:53:50,823
So, Mellie.

1415
01:53:50,825 --> 01:53:56,495
What do you make of all
this Logan curse stuff?

1416
01:53:56,497 --> 01:53:58,197
Well, that's
Clyde's thing.

1417
01:53:58,199 --> 01:54:01,667
I never really gave it
that much thought.

1418
01:54:01,669 --> 01:54:04,937
What about you?
You think we're destined
to repeat the past?

1419
01:54:06,940 --> 01:54:08,407
No.

1420
01:54:10,643 --> 01:54:12,845
I'm all about
the future.

1421
01:54:17,150 --> 01:54:20,652
Oh, shoot. Sorry about that.
Another especial for the lady?

1422
01:54:20,654 --> 01:54:22,955
Yeah. I missed out
on the toast.

1423
01:54:22,957 --> 01:54:26,491
You know they say
it's bad luck to toast
with an empty glass.

1424
01:54:26,493 --> 01:54:28,393
They do say that.

1425
01:54:28,395 --> 01:54:32,464
It's also bad luck
to toast alone, so why don't you
pour yourself one on me

1426
01:54:32,466 --> 01:54:34,766
so you don't jinx me.

1427
01:54:37,904 --> 01:54:42,007
I would've remembered
if you'd ever been
in the bar before.

1428
01:54:42,009 --> 01:54:43,909
Are you
just passin' through?
Yeah.

1429
01:54:43,911 --> 01:54:45,577
Passing through.

1430
01:54:47,213 --> 01:54:49,114
But I'm hopin'
to stay a while.

1431
01:54:51,050 --> 01:54:52,584
Well, then...

1432
01:54:54,354 --> 01:54:55,921
Here's to stayin'
a while.


